Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "project_short_name": filter to the breast‑cancer project ‘TCGA‑BRCA’.  
• "gene_type": keep only rows where the value is ‘protein_coding’.  
• "sample_type_name": locate the tissue category of each sample (e.g. “Primary Tumor”, “Solid Tissue Normal”, etc.).  
• "case_barcode": identify the individual patient / case; group on this to see how many tissue types appear for each case.  
• "sample_barcode": differentiate the many samples that can belong to one case.  
• "aliquot_barcode": separate aliquots when several expression profiles were generated from the same sample.  
• Expression columns ("fpkm_unstranded", "tpm_unstranded", …): not needed for the search itself, but can be displayed for context.  

Typical conditions that will be useful  
• WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'  
• AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'  
• AND "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%'  
• GROUP BY "case_barcode" HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows, all identifiers quoted) that gradually build toward the final query of interest.  
Adjust “TCGA”, “TCGA_VERSIONED”, and “RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35” if your database uses different capitalisation.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at 20 breast‑cancer rows to confirm column values.
SELECT *
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List the distinct tissue categories present in TCGA‑BRCA.
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_type_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show 20 BRCA samples that are annotated as “Solid Tissue Normal”.
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode",
       "sample_barcode",
       "sample_type_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Count how many different tissue types each BRCA case contains.
SELECT "case_barcode",
       COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") AS "tissue_type_count"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
ORDER BY "tissue_type_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Display each case–tissue‑type combination (one per row) for BRCA.
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode",
       "sample_type_name"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Identify cases that have BOTH “Solid Tissue Normal” AND at least one other tissue type.
SELECT "case_barcode"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
   AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Same as #6 but restricted to rows where the gene is protein‑coding.
SELECT "case_barcode"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
   AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Bring back extra context (one row per sample) for the cases that meet #7.
SELECT t."case_barcode",
       t."sample_barcode",
       t."sample_type_name",
       t."gene_name",
       t."tpm_unstranded"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35" t
WHERE t."project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND t."gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
  AND t."case_barcode" IN (
        SELECT "case_barcode"
        FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
          AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
        GROUP BY "case_barcode"
        HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
           AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Aggregate the list of tissue types observed per case (string aggregation).
SELECT "case_barcode",
       LISTAGG(DISTINCT "sample_type_name", ', ') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY "sample_type_name") AS "tissue_types"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
   AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final concise list of BRCA cases that have RNA‑seq for multiple tissue types, one being “Solid Tissue Normal” (protein‑coding rows only).
SELECT DISTINCT "case_barcode"
FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "gene_type" = 'protein_coding'
  AND "case_barcode" IN (
        SELECT "case_barcode"
        FROM "TCGA"."TCGA_VERSIONED"."RNASEQ_HG38_GDC_R35"
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
        GROUP BY "case_barcode"
        HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "sample_type_name") > 1
           AND SUM(CASE WHEN "sample_type_name" ILIKE '%Solid%Tissue%Normal%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) > 0
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

